  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A spherical mirror is obtained as shown in the figure from a hollow glass sphere, if an object is positioned in front&nbsp;of the mirror, what will be the nature and magnification of the image of the object? (Figure down&nbsp;as schematic and not to scale)</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/dd15d9ae-2714-4162-a3ed-be7ba83e4a53-image.png\" style=\"width: 307px; height: 185px;\" />&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "H2MDU",
      "text": "Inverted, real and magnified",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "rT0Ev",
      "text": "Erect, virtual and magnified",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "KIgEb",
      "text": "Erect, virutual and unmagnified",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kn2Vx",
      "text": "Inverted, real and unmagnified",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The image will form between&nbsp;the focus and centre&nbsp;of&nbsp;the concave mirror when we keep the object between the&nbsp;centre and infinity.It will be real image.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/955e21b1-2176-49e1-abdc-b62d9ebb2dc5-image.png\" style=\"width: 312px; height: 236px;\" /></p>",
